kage**  \n   ```bash\n   go test ./pkg\n   ```\n\n3. **Run a single test function**  \n   ```bash\n   go test -run TestParse -v\n   ```\n\n4. **Check coverage**  \n   ```bash\n   go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...\n   go tool cover -html=coverage.out\n   ```\n\n5. **Detect races**  \n   ```bash\n   go test -race ./...\n   ```\n\n6. **Run benchmarks**  \n   ```bash\n   go test -bench=. -benchmem ./pkg\n   ```\n\nThese commands will execute the tests that are already written in the repository. If you add new tests, they will automatically be picked up by the `go test ./...` command."
